  "title": "Two Melbourne Children Suffer Kidney Failure After E. coli Infections Linked to Petting Farm Visits",
  "summary": "Two young children in Melbourne have reportedly suffered severe health complications after contracting Shiga toxin-producing E. coli (STEC), with both cases linked to visits to the same petting farm. One child reportedly developed kidney failure and spent more than two weeks receiving dialysis, while another has suffered serious complications, including permanent brain damage. The cases have raised renewed concerns about the potential health risks associated with contact with animals at petting",
